    "No query-specific nucleoside transporter, BCRP efflux, or intestinal metabolism data; L5 records are for other nucleoside analogs.",
    "Fasted-state human data for the exact query are absent; closest fasting records are C10 and C07.",
    "C05 (OGT719) shows considerable interpatient variability and no fasting condition.",
    "C66 is a calculated value assuming Fa=1 and Fg=1, limiting its transferability."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction high: the most relevant L1 human nucleoside records (zalcitabine 80%, ddA/ddl 38%, OGT719 ~25%) and L2 nucleoside analog F values all exceed 20%; L3/L4 support oral absorption of polar nucleosides; L5 adds mixed mechanistic transporter/efflux evidence for other nucleoside analogs; L6 adds low-to-moderate hepatic intrinsic clearance for purine/nucleoside analogs and no query-specific high first-pass evidence. Confidence remains moderate because the exact query lacks direct F data."
}

